{"agency_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0SnSoMAnYKI", "captured_at": "2026-06-25T07:48:34+00:00", "content": "Bennett and Pepa's Story: Navigating sepsis diagnosis in Aotearoa\n\nBennett Pomana and his wife Pepa share their experience of navigating sepsis diagnosis in Aotearoa New Zealand. Bennett's sepsis journey started when he became ill in December 2022. He spent 10 days in an induced coma in Wellington Regional Hospital's intensive care unit. In this video, the couple talk about Bennett’s ongoing health issues and what can be done to support those diagnosed with sepsis and their families.", "content_hash": "a605d47caeafbea5c4237040ad594f8cc631905859df30ae3891bf444b485b7d", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission-youtube-a1b00f74", "video_id": "0SnSoMAnYKI"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-10-24T20:58:04+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-10\\112b76f822f94c279100b6f7.json", "record_id": "youtube:112b76f822f94c279100b6f7", "source_account": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q"}
{"agency_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pIIm9XRAmpQ", "captured_at": "2026-06-25T07:48:34+00:00", "content": "Olivia and Karen’s story\n\nWhen Olivia and Karen found a midwife who specialised in supporting rainbow families they said, ‘Sign us up’. The two mothers share the importance of inclusive language and of both parents being included in the whole pregnancy and birth experience. \n\nGo to www.hqsc.govt.nz/AotearoaPatientSafetyDay2024 for the accessible transcript and to watch our other videos", "content_hash": "afc7dd6a6cf276a7f9559a4db835ed512eeec92e8c256f22605895ff0231bbc3", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission-youtube-a1b00f74", "video_id": "pIIm9XRAmpQ"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-10-17T21:56:39+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-10\\fccb5fa0fbceca51af2971ea.json", "record_id": "youtube:fccb5fa0fbceca51af2971ea", "source_account": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q"}
{"agency_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hWIBRtW46cY", "captured_at": "2026-06-25T07:48:34+00:00", "content": "Petala's story\n\nPetala was anxious when she found out she was pregnant. She wanted a Pacific Island midwife as she says coming from a Samoan family she thrives on community. Petala talks about the need for education around pregnancy and sex in the Pacific community. \n\nGo to www.hqsc.govt.nz/AotearoaPatientSafetyDay2024 for the accessible transcript.", "content_hash": "f618ea5ad7023f56f7b38e1dd1bd4d2ddc8480a71aa449492184bd5ac7511b4f", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission-youtube-a1b00f74", "video_id": "hWIBRtW46cY"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-10-17T21:46:49+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-10\\d5e75f89d3bcf39eab46b2dd.json", "record_id": "youtube:d5e75f89d3bcf39eab46b2dd", "source_account": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q"}
{"agency_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z8J3RH_Dww0", "captured_at": "2026-06-25T07:48:34+00:00", "content": "Phoenix’s story\n\nFor Phoenix, having her cultural needs incorporated into her pregnancy and birth experience made all the difference. \n\nHaving two midwives who listened to her and ensured her whānau were involved in every step of the process means, looking back, she doesn’t so much remember the pain but rather having her father holding her up, her Nana’s karakia, her partner catching the baby, and her mother cutting the baby Āiorangi’s cord with muka ties woven by her grandmother. \n\nPhoenix had the birth she wanted because she had two midwives who listened to her.\n\nGo to www.hqsc.govt.nz/AotearoaPatientSafetyDay2024 for the accessible transcript.", "content_hash": "1af95841c46602dee4740e934d7ed0f7690f2b6e08f909a0dbb09b579676146a", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission-youtube-a1b00f74", "video_id": "z8J3RH_Dww0"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-10-17T21:43:16+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-10\\4d559af9fcde6224901e29ec.json", "record_id": "youtube:4d559af9fcde6224901e29ec", "source_account": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q"}
{"agency_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0WSINbVUycc", "captured_at": "2026-06-25T07:48:34+00:00", "content": "Robyn's story\n\nAssociate professor of midwifery and lead maternity care midwife Robyn Maude has 46 years of experience. \n\nShe talks about the partnership model used in Aotearoa New Zealand, which is based on trust and reciprocity, building relationships and having informed choice and consent. \n\nRobyn says you need to ask people you’re working with right from day one, ‘What are the things you need to keep you culturally safe during your pregnancy?’\n\nGo to www.hqsc.govt.nz/AotearoaPatientSafetyDay2024 for the accessible transcript and to find more resources for Te Rā Haumaru Tūroro o Aotearoa | Aotearoa Patient Safety Day 2024.", "content_hash": "75a1eccf2d5c826426e75546422afc032575cbb92ce0ffc32e703db097b2860c", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_id": "health-quality-and-safety-commission-youtube-a1b00f74", "video_id": "0WSINbVUycc"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-10-17T21:02:28+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-10\\da613d1c6ee05442c2946102.json", "record_id": "youtube:da613d1c6ee05442c2946102", "source_account": "UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5yFtbreIu20QxZMb4v7L7Q"}
